  "description": "ReActive Adaptations has been receiving requests for it’s creation for years. The only of its kind on the market, this three-wheeled foot-pedaled recumbent is an actual off-road demon. With 24-inch front wheels and a 26″ rear wheel capped in the meanest knobbies, the Stinger has the ground clearance and traction enough to conquer any rocky, root-filled trail in your back yard or the mountains. Though the real key here is the derailleur. Other tadpole recumbents on the market available to the “off road” world often have low hanging derailleurs. Mounted on the 26-inch rear wheel, the Stinger’s derailleur is free from many trail collisions that leave its predecessors stranded. In addition to 26-inch wheels, the Stinger is composed of an ADI Active Contour seat back for optimum positioning and comfort, carbon fiber seat pan, and adjustable single speed foot cranks. The optional 14-speed Rohloff Speedhub is available to rescue your ride at the bottom of all the steepest hills, and the new heavy duty Tektro hydraulic disc brakes are there to control your speed on the way back down!",
